<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Syrian Treaty of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Syrian Treaty of Independence was negotiated in 1936 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Syrian nationalists of the National Bloc after a long general strike. It promised Syrian independence within a few years and joined the Alawite State and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal Druze</a> to the Syrian Republic, while preserving French military and economic privileges. The French parliament never ratified it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> became fully independent only in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-treaty-of-independence.jpg" alt="Franco-Syrian Treaty of Independence" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Historian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_National_Bloc_signing_the_FrancoSyrian_Treaty.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
